Z||000000||mrfixit58||04-14-2000||06:17 PM||||Well guys, you'll never believe me when I tell you that I've been out zipping around in so I'll tell ya. An all original 88 GT, 5-speed, Yellow with T-Top. There is only a few made with this combo in the WHOLE WORLD. WHAT A PUMP!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">:<P>I met this girl about a year ago and struck up a conversation about her Yellow GT. I told here if she ever decided to sell, let me know. I gave her one on my business cards and left.<P>She has called me a couple of times about various things that needed to be done to her car but, at the time, I couldn't help her out. The other day she called me to ask if I knew anything about the Fiero headlights (that's when I turned to you guys for advise). Seems she paid some garage $300 to fix the other headlight last year and really didn't want to do that again.<P>I told her I could help and she brought it over this morning. Of course, all it needs is a $5 headlight kit from Rodney (which is on order, by the way). I'm not charging her anything. I'm just telling her to consider it a $300 down payment.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>She told me her husband was embarrassed that she called me for help but she told him, and I quote: "Why not, he is going to wind up with it anyway??". CAN YOU BELIEVE IT! I just may have to take a few pictures of it, just so you guys will believe me.<P>Way too excited,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
